- P-33 **The work toward microGPT compiled follows the phases, in the order that the curator approved.** Phase 3, the compiled checker reports no error on the interpreter's whole library (the distance to the switch-over at zero; F-53 defines it and holds its value); phase 4, the switch-over, first the natives, the library's `builtinPrimitive` bindings made to run on the compiled path, then the compiled path reads the interpreter's library and the compiler's prelude is deleted; phase 5, microGPT compiles: its static types, the array design and the code generator's open gaps; phase 6, microGPT runs fast. Other work has gone in beside that order. The repair batch from the reviews of the landed batches went in before phase 3: on 2026-09-27 he said that those reviews could yield batches that go in before phase 3. Code-generator work goes on under either library (P-37). One decision that an agent took without his approval: row 320 has two halves. The agent fixed one, mutability across the api, and gated the other as an expected failure instead of fixing it (`ProjectFortress/compiler_tests/XXXExportVarRungXLinked`): an api implemented by a component of another name does not link.
